# UI style

- Use the `Theme` colors and the `Painter` styles for cards, buttons and fields. Cards are 168 px wide; semantic state also needs text, icon, or outline instead of color alone.
- Use `ScreenGeometry` as the single source for panel, header, tabs, toolbar, viewport, content, and slot origins. Compact mode is 196 px below 420 logical pixels; wide mode is 384 px at and above 420. The panel height is fixed at `ScreenGeometry.PANEL_HEIGHT` (256) GUI pixels, so the menu scales only with the Minecraft GUI scale; a shorter screen caps it to the available height.
- Header, primary tabs, and toolbar stay fixed. Only the viewport content scrolls, and resizing must preserve the active page and stable control focus.
- Keep `ScreenHandler` slot coordinates immutable. `DreamTableScreen.x/y` are the current slot origin; slot drawing, highlighting, tooltips, and hit testing must use that origin and reject every partially clipped slot.
- The four primary tabs are persistent. Build owns catalog/work/material flows, Farms owns finished-farm operations and Keep Loaded, Schematics owns imports, and Settings owns client/build preferences.
- Custom-drawn interactive elements must register stable `ControlId` values and expose a vanilla widget for focus and narration. Mouse and keyboard activation must invoke the same page action.
- Draw text without shadow on the cream panel. Vanilla text fields draw with shadow, so use them only for input, as `SearchBox` does.
- Destructive actions, such as discarding a started build, need a second click.
- Keyboard focus is always visible: after Tab or arrow navigation the focused card, button, chip or tab gets a three-layer ring (navy, white, theme cyan, `Painter.focusRing`) drawn inside its bounds, from the vanilla focus of its `UiControl` (`PageContext.setFocusedControl`, set by the screen each frame). It hides after a mouse click, like vanilla. Focus never moves to a control that is scrolled out of the content area. A disabled control narrates "Unavailable" once, followed by its own reason when it has one.
- A "click again" arming hint (Discard, Take Down) is an information notice (`ScreenActions.hint`), not a red problem. Per-frame layout math (wrapped text heights, filtered lists) is computed once per change of its inputs and has no side effects such as network requests; requests are sent from `draw` only and retried on a timer until answered.
- Clipboard icons use each item's own model, facing forward, at the 2D icon size.
- Clipboard page arrows play the book page-turn sound.
- Tooltips are only for controls that show no text of their own: the icon-only compact tabs and item/material slots. A control with a visible label, card detail or button detail (cards, buttons, chips, expanded tabs, option toggles) never has a hover tooltip, because its text scrolls and is fully readable; a tooltip must never repeat a title already on screen. Anything a player needs to know, such as why a control is disabled or why a file was rejected, is shown as the card or button detail line, never only in a tooltip. Pages draw no tooltips; the ones that exist go through `screen/ui/Tooltips` (wrapped to `Tooltips.maxWidth`, never wider than half the window, drawn with vanilla's positioner so it stays inside the screen); never call `DrawContext.drawTooltip` with unwrapped `Text` lines. `TooltipPolicyTest` guards this.
- Labels and subtitles (header, tabs, cards, buttons, chips) go through `Painter.fitted`: text that fits is drawn as is, longer text scrolls inside its box like a vanilla button (`Marquee`), so no important text is cut with "..." or readable only in a tooltip. A button may carry a second, smaller detail line (`PageContext.button` with a detail), used for a delivery hint or the reason it is disabled.
- Messages to the player from the table, build, farms and protection use the table notice, not the action bar: `TableNoticePayload.send/info/problem` on the server (falls back to the action bar when `ServerNetwork.canSend` is false) and `TableNotices.show/info/problem` on the client. It is centered at the top for 5 seconds with a 1 second fade, drawn as a translucent panel (about 58% dark fill, softer 70% outline, `NoticeShape`) with pixel-rounded corners (3 pixels cut from each corner) and fully opaque text, the newest replaces the older, success and information are green and problems, warnings and alerts are red with a matching outline. The HUD draws it, and `DreamTableScreen` draws it on top of itself. Messages meant to stay in the chat log keep `sendMessage(..., false)`.
- While the local player's own build or repair runs and the table's chunk is loaded on the client, the notice slot also shows a persistent, live "Building n/total" line (with the time left when the table menu has reported the build's rate), green, without timer or fade (`BuildProgressLine`, `NoticeBoard.setPersistent`). An ordinary notice shows over it for its 5 seconds and the line comes back afterwards. It is not drawn over the table menu (the Work page shows the same progress) or with F1, and disappears when the build finishes, pauses, is blocked, discarded, or the player leaves the chunk or world.
- Farm alerts have no page of their own: a farm with an active alert is marked with a red warning sign before its name in My Farms (`AlertText.listName`, from `FarmLoader.Entry.alerts`), and its page ends with one red "Alert: ..." line per active alert (`AlertText.lines`).
